# GitHub Actions Strategy

## Hard Limits

| Resource | Limit | Our Usage | % Used |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| GitHub Actions minutes (private repo) | 2,000/month | 1,440/month | 72% |
| currentsapi | 1,000 req/day | 48/day | 4.8% |
| newsdata.io | 200 credits/day | 18/day | 9% |
| contextualweb.io | 10,000 req/month | 540/month | 5.4% |
| RSS feeds (25) | Unlimited | 1,200/day | FREE |

## Two-Tier Schedule

```
cron: '*/30 * * * *'   ← every 30 minutes

TIER 1 (every run — freshness):
  → currentsapi latest headlines (1 API call)
  → All 25 Hindi RSS feeds (parallel, free)

TIER 2 (every 4 hours — volume):
  → newsdata.io: sports, technology, business (3 calls)
  → contextualweb: health, science, entertainment (3 calls)
```

## Rotation (daily totals)

| Provider | Calls/Day | Cost |
|----------|-----------|------|
| currentsapi | 48 | 4.8% of 1,000 |
| newsdata.io | 18 credits | 9% of 200 |
| contextualweb | 18 calls | 5.4% of 333/day |
| RSS feeds | 1,200 fetches | Free |
| Firebase writes | ~40–80 bundle docs | <0.5% of 20,000 |
| GitHub Actions | ~48 min/day | 72% of 2,000/month |

## Content Pipeline (fetch_news.py)

```
Fetch (3 API providers + 25 RSS) → Normalize → Dedup (3-layer) → Bundle (≤30/doc) → upload_bundles() → article_bundles
```

Short field names in each bundle: `i`=id, `t`=title, `d`=description, `img`=imageUrl, `u`=articleUrl, `p`=publishedAt (ms), `s`=sourceName, `c`=category

### Deduplication Layers
1. **Article ID hash** — SHA-256 of (normalized_title + normalized_source)
2. **URL dedup** — seen_urls set within RSS processing
3. **Cross-run cache** — `.article_cache.json` persisted via actions/cache

### Provider Tagging
Every article gets `_provider` key (`currentsapi` / `rss` / `newsdata` / `contextualweb`).
Stripped before Firebase upload (short field mapping in `upload_bundles`).

### Category Short Codes (CATEGORY_SHORT dict)
API source categories are normalized then mapped to short codes: `nat`, `pol`, `bus`, `spt`, `ent`, `tec`, `hlt`, `int`, `cri`, `edu`, `sci`, `def`, `stk`.
RSS feeds use short codes directly in their `category` field.

